WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.916
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:14.520
PRESENTER: Before I
introduce today's speaker,

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.630
I wanted to say a word or
two about two great friends

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:22.230
of the department, Neil
and Jane Pappalardo.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:30.960
Five years ago or so, the
MIT physics department

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.720
realized that we
had an opportunity

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:39.090
to join a consortium
to build two telescopes

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.350
on a mountaintop in Chile.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.480
And we really wanted
to do this and couldn't

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.850
see any way to do it.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:53.200
Neil and Jane Pappalardo
decided to help us do that.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:01:00.990
And this December, Neil and
Jane and 350 close friends

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.570
gather together on the top
of this mountain in Chile

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:06.540
to have a celebration for the
inauguration of the Magellan

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:14.190
telescopes, truly magnificent
instruments, state of the art

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:18.420
telescopes which really
put us in the vanguard

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:19.710
of optical astronomy.

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.530
Then two years
ago, Neil and Jane

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.560
decided to help us
create a distinguished

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.960
post-doctoral program following
the model of the Junior

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.270
Fellows at Harvard.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:39.780
And we began this in
the physics department.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.600
And now we have this
year, for the first time,

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.760
three Pappalardo Fellows.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:50.580
And there'll be another three
joining us next September.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:56.730
This is really a wonderful
thing because over time,

00:01:56.730 --> 00:01:58.710
we hope it will grow
into a program that

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.812
spans the School of Science.

00:02:00.812 --> 00:02:02.520
Some of the other
departments are already

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.120
beginning to follow our example.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:07.950
So there are a couple of
other Science Fellows.

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:11.890
And this kind of
program is wonderful

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:16.650
because it gives the opportunity
for brilliant young people

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:20.010
to do something that they
want to do that they think

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.710
is interesting on their
own, or in collaboration

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:24.900
with other people at MIT.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:31.620
So Neil and Jane have helped
us in getting our hands

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.640
on absolutely
frontier technology,

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.780
and also getting our hands on
absolutely fantastic people.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:42.900
And those are the two things
you need to do great science,

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:43.980
and certainly in physics.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:47.730
You need great technology
and great people.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:50.850
And so I'd like to just take
a moment now to ask all of you

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:53.910
to join me in thanking Neil
and Jane for what they've

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.298
done for us.

00:02:55.298 --> 00:02:59.210
[APPLAUSE]

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:12.060
Now, speaking of great people
who make great physics,

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:15.240
it's time to
introduce this year's

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:20.070
distinguished
Pappalardo lecturer.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:23.190
And you already have
a nice little summary

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:30.150
in here, which tells you a
little bit about Frank Wilczek.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:32.640
Frank was just a kid
when he and David Gross

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:36.670
discovered asymptotic freedom.

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:42.270
This is really a critical, a
key aspect of our understanding

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.260
of the strong force.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:48.700
He's made great
contributions, of course,

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:51.930
to our understanding
of the standard model,

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:56.700
to cosmology, to
condensed matter physics.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:05.010
So he is truly an unusually
broad and deep physicist.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.840
Furthermore, he
and his wife Betsy

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:11.970
wrote a magnificent book on
modern physics for the layman.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:16.440
And he writes these wonderful
articles in Physics Today which

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:20.579
really are very deep, and
yet, at the same time,

00:04:20.579 --> 00:04:23.900
understandable.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:25.940
Frank is interested
in everything

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:29.000
and he understands everything.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:34.460
So it's appropriate that he
speak today about everything.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.916
It's all yours.

00:04:35.916 --> 00:04:39.860
[APPLAUSE]

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:48.241
WILCZEK: Thank you.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:58.070
I like to think of Pythagoras
as the first modern physicist.

00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:02.960
Certainly, he made one
of the first discoveries

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:04.700
of a physical law
in the modern sense,

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.926
and that is a quantitative--

00:05:06.926 --> 00:05:13.540
no-- fact about observable
realities of nature.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.970
It's a very beautiful
law, and in a way,

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:20.380
it's a law that, to this
day, is not fully understood.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:25.090
It's the law that the notes
that we see as harmonious are

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.780
the notes where the
length of a string--

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:30.188
he was the first
string theorist, also--

00:05:30.188 --> 00:05:34.030
[LAUGHTER]

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:38.500
If you have different lengths of
string of the same composition

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:42.100
and under the same
tension, then the strings

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:46.600
will sound harmonious to
our ears when plucked if

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:51.970
and only if their lengths are
in simple numerical ratios.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:54.220
So if the ratio of
the length is 2 to 1,

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.130
we'll hear them as
being an octave.

00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.170
If it's 2 to 3,
we'll hear a fifth.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:01.280
4 to 3, a fourth, and so on.

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:09.910
Well, being a
modern physicist, he

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:12.010
was very impressed
with his work,

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:16.530
and generalized it
to the principal

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:20.190
that all things are number,
that a complete description

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:24.564
of the world should be based
on numerical relationships.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:33.190
This is what I think of
as the Pythagorean vision,

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:38.380
or, in modern language, the idea
that, as John Wheeler put it,

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:40.680
you get its from bits.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:46.990
From purely conceptual
information theoretic notions,

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:50.260
if you like, you get a
valid description of nature.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:58.720
That idea was profoundly
influential and inspiring

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:02.770
to the followers of Pythagoras
in physics, and especially

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.870
in astrology.

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:10.260
And one of the people who
made great contributions, both

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:14.380
to physics and astrology,
was Johannes Kepler,

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:17.980
who perhaps represented
the apogee of Pythagorean

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:23.470
thinking up until his day.

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:26.290
We learn in physics textbooks
about Kepler's three laws

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:32.610
of planetary motion, the
first, second, and third laws.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:36.060
But less well known is
that there was a zeroth law

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:38.880
that he proposed that was the
first law of planetary motion

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:44.660
that he described, which
is entirely fallacious,

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:48.240
but which inspired his career
and was very Pythagorean.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:52.350
His idea was that the different
distances-- well, first of all,

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:56.580
that the planets moved around
the sun in circular orbits,

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.370
and secondly, that the
sizes of those orbits

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:03.030
was fixed by circumscribing
and inscribing

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:05.830
the different regular solids.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:08.860
So if I remember
correctly, there's

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:11.560
an icosahedron around
the innermost sphere.

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:17.220
And the sphere that
carries Mercury

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.780
is inscribed around
that icosahedron.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:22.030
Then there's an octahedron
then a dodecahedron.

00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:26.470
Then you can see the
tetrahedron and the cube.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:30.010
And all these spheres
rotated carrying the planets

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:30.820
around them.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:33.909
And as they rotated,
emitted musical notes,

00:08:33.909 --> 00:08:37.168
which Kepler even figured out.

00:08:37.168 --> 00:08:41.080
[LAUGHTER]

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:50.160
Well, soon after, Kepler
went from the zeroth law

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.740
to the first law.

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:54.990
And according to the first
law of planetary motion, which

00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:58.380
he abstracted from the
observational data of Tycho

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:03.130
Brahe, the planets actually
move around the sun in ellipses.

00:09:03.130 --> 00:09:07.740
So this beautiful construction
was to his credit,

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:10.892
immediately abandoned by him.

00:09:10.892 --> 00:09:18.790
And this kind of idea that
the structure of matter

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:28.370
in the universe was dictated by
purely conceptual constructions

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:34.620
like regular solids, went into
an eclipse that lasted, really,

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:38.330
for 250 years.

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:40.650
In Newtonian mechanics
and classical mechanics,

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:45.510
which replaced Kepler's
early speculations,

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:49.090
the orbits of the planets
are largely arbitrary.

00:09:49.090 --> 00:09:52.200
If you take the sizes of the
different orbits of the planets

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.540
and a star came by
our solar system,

00:09:54.540 --> 00:10:00.690
the orbits would all change
and life would go on.

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:05.850
In fact, now we've even observed
extra solar planetary systems.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:09.300
And they don't necessarily look
at all like our solar system.

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:21.420
In classical mechanics, and even
in classical electrodynamics,

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:28.370
this Pythagorean, Keplerian idea
that the structure of matter

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:31.220
is uniquely dictated
by conceptual elements

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:33.830
just doesn't hold.

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:36.410
Technically it's
because the equations

00:10:36.410 --> 00:10:38.570
of classical mechanics
and also the equations

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:42.650
of electrodynamics fix no
particular scale of size.

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:46.100
If you take those equations
and multiply all the distance

00:10:46.100 --> 00:10:48.860
scale by a constant, you
get the same equations.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:50.890
So you map solutions
into solutions.

00:10:50.890 --> 00:10:52.670
There can be nothing
that fixes the size

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.950
of particular materials,
and certainly nothing

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:57.770
that would lead to chemistry,
to lead to atoms of different

00:10:57.770 --> 00:11:00.260
or materials of different
types in different places

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:05.040
in the universe being put
together the same way.

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:09.090
And that's really
the way it stood

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:15.810
until the early part
of the 20th century,

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:23.400
when especially in the
work of Niels Bohr,

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:26.880
the Pythagorean and Keplerian
ideas made a big comeback.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:38.980
Bohr's original atomic
model was, in fact,

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:41.560
based on an analogy
to the solar system.

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:43.630
It was based on 1
over r squared forces,

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:46.600
electrical not
gravitational, but satisfying

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:48.010
mechanical equations.

00:11:48.010 --> 00:11:50.890
But he added the extra
element, very reminiscent

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.710
of Kepler, that
only certain sizes

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:57.940
of orbits, only certain sizes
orbits, actually occurred.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:04.224
But this time it's right, or
at least a fair approximation.

00:12:07.402 --> 00:12:08.650
I'm looking for a pointer.

00:12:14.637 --> 00:12:15.137
Ah.

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:18.860
Okay.

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:22.940
So you had different
possible orbits and electrons

00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:25.890
in the atom could only
orbit in one particular way.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:29.630
Then there was some kind of
mysterious non-causal process

00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:31.940
where they could hop from
one orbit to another.

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:34.356
And you're not supposed to ask
where they were in between.

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:40.850
By reasoning like this, which
Einstein called the highest

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:43.550
form of musicality in
the sphere of thought,

00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:47.840
somehow referring back to
the music of the spheres

00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:53.410
and the discrete
relationships, Bohr

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:55.780
got a successful description
of the spectral lines

00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:59.530
and their frequency,
which I've written

00:12:59.530 --> 00:13:03.040
down here as an equation.

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:05.920
The details of the equations
aren't so important for us.

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:12.640
But I want to emphasize how
closely the idea of capturing

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:18.010
reality in terms of purely
conceptual notions-- that is,

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:19.750
ultimately numerical notions--

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:23.500
is realized in this formula
for the spectral lines.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:25.360
Almost everything in
it, everything in blue

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:27.590
here is a number.

00:13:27.590 --> 00:13:30.860
4 is certainly a number.

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:31.720
Pi is a number.

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:37.070
c, the speed of light, well,
that's an honorary number.

00:13:42.690 --> 00:13:44.460
Why do I say it's
an honorary number?

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:47.550
Well, in the theory of
special relativity, which

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:50.640
is a deep, foundational
theory of physics,

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:54.160
we have a symmetry
between space and time.

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:56.650
Transformations,
symmetry transformations,

00:13:56.650 --> 00:13:59.920
that allow us to mix up space
and time, the so-called Lorentz

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:01.100
transformations.

00:14:03.636 --> 00:14:05.760
But space and time are
measured in different units.

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:12.330
So we have to have some
conversion factor that

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:20.950
converts those physically
identical objects, objects

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:25.930
related by a symmetry,
into the same units.

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:29.950
And that's what this
conversion factor does.

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:32.710
So you should think of it
as being like the three that

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:34.010
converts yards into feet.

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:41.580
Similarly, h bar,
Planck's constant,

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:43.890
can be thought of as
an honorary number

00:14:43.890 --> 00:14:46.660
because in the deep theory
of quantum mechanics,

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:50.130
there is a relationship
between energy and frequency.

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:53.130
The energy of
oscillations is related--

00:14:53.130 --> 00:14:55.020
the energy associated
with an oscillation

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:58.770
is related to the frequency
at which it occurs in time.

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:02.730
But energy and time are
measured in different units.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:04.350
We need a conversion factor.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:06.540
And that's Planck's constant.

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:09.940
Okay.

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:11.500
These n's are different numbers.

00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:16.970
They describe the
different orbits.

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:20.650
And then we have some
things that are not numbers,

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:24.410
whether honorary or actual.

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:26.670
But there aren't
very many of them.

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:29.360
There's alpha, the
so-called fine structure

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:35.270
constant, numerically
equal to about 1/136,

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:39.290
which describes the absolute
strength with which protons

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:42.624
and electrons
attract one another.

00:15:42.624 --> 00:15:44.540
So this is just telling
you about the strength

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.250
of the electrical forces.

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:48.620
And then we have a
mass factor, mass

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:51.110
of the electron times
the mass of the proton,

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:53.300
divided by the sum of the two.

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:56.966
This is almost equal to just
the mass of the electron

00:15:56.966 --> 00:15:58.340
because the mass
of the proton is

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:00.860
much bigger and almost
cancels between numerator

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:04.450
and denominator.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:09.110
Okay, so that's hydrogen,
and this physical spectrum

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.480
of hydrogen reduced
to almost purely

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:14.510
conceptual numerical elements.

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:18.950
In fact, it is reduced in
a very good approximation,

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:20.660
if we take the
mass of the proton

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:23.090
to be very large
compared to the electron,

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:27.290
to just two non-numerical
elements, that

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:30.320
is the mass of the electron and
the fine structure constant.

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:38.990
That's hydrogen. And
hydrogen described

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:41.870
in Bohr's provisional
theory, or Bohr's theory,

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:44.880
which was just a way station
to modern quantum mechanics.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:01.560
The successor theory to
Bohr's theory of atoms,

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:04.030
modern quantum
mechanics, is based

00:17:04.030 --> 00:17:11.109
not on a picture of electrons
as particles circling in orbits,

00:17:11.109 --> 00:17:16.359
but rather electrons as
waves which oscillate

00:17:16.359 --> 00:17:19.369
up and down around the proton--

00:17:19.369 --> 00:17:21.349
yes, oscillate up and
down around the proton,

00:17:21.349 --> 00:17:26.260
which has captured them in
different states of excitation.

00:17:26.260 --> 00:17:31.080
And this is a beautiful
shareware program by Dean

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:38.230
[? Dowager ?] which shows
the different energy

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:41.350
levels, the different
stationary states of hydrogen,

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:46.120
how the electron behaves
in the modern analog

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:48.530
of these different orbitals.

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:50.003
It's Mac only.

00:17:50.003 --> 00:17:53.950
[LAUGHTER]

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:57.500
And it's a beautiful thing.

00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:00.490
In fact, it also allows you
to play microcosmic God.

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:03.020
You can grab the atom
and spin it around.

00:18:03.020 --> 00:18:06.430
You can-- well,
fortunately, what

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:10.270
I see on my screen is much
better than what you see.

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:12.280
You can spin it around.

00:18:12.280 --> 00:18:14.860
You can make
different transitions.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:17.270
So here let's
transit down there.

00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:19.060
See, that's this line here.

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:23.746
And this is the real thing.

00:18:23.746 --> 00:18:25.620
This is actually being
computed in real time.

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:28.610
This is what
electrons actually do.

00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:31.400
This is what we're made out of.

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:37.530
This is our most accurate
description of atomic nature.

00:18:37.530 --> 00:18:38.540
And it only depends--

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:40.630
all this only--
this is hydrogen.

00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:42.570
If you also go to more
complicated atoms,

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:47.340
if you go to
molecules, all you need

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:49.780
is the mass of the
electron and alpha.

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:53.430
So those are the two
first ingredients

00:18:53.430 --> 00:18:55.640
in our numerical
recipe for nature.

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:08.970
So by 1930 or so, modern
quantum mechanics was in place.

00:19:13.240 --> 00:19:21.150
And attention switched to
describing those atomic nuclei,

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:23.250
the protons and the
more complicated

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:27.070
atomic nuclei in bigger atoms.

00:19:27.070 --> 00:19:29.070
Well, first of all, I
showed you the wave atoms.

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:31.960
And I think you'll agree,
you get a lot of structure

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:34.180
and a lot of physics out
of just these two numbers.

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:39.900
But this was approximate.

00:19:39.900 --> 00:19:43.680
We had to neglect or take the
mass of the proton to infinity.

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:49.020
And similarly, we'd have
to put in from experiment

00:19:49.020 --> 00:19:51.510
the masses of other nuclei if
we wanted to really account

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:54.810
for matter in full accuracy.

00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:59.990
So it's only an approximate
recipe for nature,

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:02.330
even for ordinary matter.

00:20:02.330 --> 00:20:06.860
And the attention of physicists
starting in 1930 or so

00:20:06.860 --> 00:20:11.030
switched or began to
focus on doing justice

00:20:11.030 --> 00:20:13.940
to those atomic nuclei inside.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:16.790
The first great breakthrough
in understanding

00:20:16.790 --> 00:20:19.190
that was the
discovery by Chadwick

00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:24.130
in 1932 of the neutron
and the swift emergence

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:26.860
of the modern picture
that nuclei are basically

00:20:26.860 --> 00:20:31.810
weakly bound assemblages
of protons and neutrons.

00:20:31.810 --> 00:20:33.330
But then it emerged--

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:37.690
and in this development,
crucial experiments

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:41.690
were done by Friedman,
Kendall, and Taylor

00:20:41.690 --> 00:20:44.110
in an MIT collaboration--

00:20:44.110 --> 00:20:46.450
that protons had
internal structure,

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:50.440
that they're not simple
objects, but are assembled out

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:54.230
of some kind of
simpler structure.

00:20:54.230 --> 00:21:00.340
And then, in a
complicated history,

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:03.960
which fortunately has an outcome
that's much simpler to describe

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:08.350
than the history, we arrived
at the modern understanding

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:10.660
of what holds protons
and neutrons-- what

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:12.580
protons and neutrons
are made out of,

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:15.040
what holds them
together, and what

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:19.330
holds more complicated
atomic nuclei together.

00:21:19.330 --> 00:21:24.050
This theory is called quantum
chromodynamics, or QCD.

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:30.290
In quantum
chromodynamics or QCD,

00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:34.820
we describe the stuff
that makes protons

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:37.970
in terms of two different
flavors of quarks,

00:21:37.970 --> 00:21:40.430
the U and the D
quarks, each of which

00:21:40.430 --> 00:21:43.607
comes in three so-called colors.

00:21:43.607 --> 00:21:45.190
They're actually
red, white, and blue.

00:21:45.190 --> 00:21:49.550
But the white was not
suitable for the transparency.

00:21:49.550 --> 00:21:52.250
So you should imagine that
these are white quarks.

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:59.060
And a bunch of gluons.

00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:00.890
Now, these are just symbols.

00:22:00.890 --> 00:22:04.070
And clearly, I'm
just joking when

00:22:04.070 --> 00:22:05.750
I say that they're colored.

00:22:05.750 --> 00:22:08.810
What this color really means
is not, of course, the color

00:22:08.810 --> 00:22:12.410
you would see it of physical
light of these quarks.

00:22:12.410 --> 00:22:14.510
Color is actually
a generalization

00:22:14.510 --> 00:22:16.610
of electromagnetic charge.

00:22:16.610 --> 00:22:18.320
It's more to be
thought of as a charge.

00:22:18.320 --> 00:22:21.740
QCD is a generalization,
a vast generalization,

00:22:21.740 --> 00:22:24.320
of quantum electrodynamics,
of the theory

00:22:24.320 --> 00:22:27.350
of electrical and
magnetic forces.

00:22:27.350 --> 00:22:29.090
Whereas electrical
and magnetic forces

00:22:29.090 --> 00:22:30.650
are based on electric
charge, these

00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:33.440
are based on the three
kinds of charges,

00:22:33.440 --> 00:22:35.600
all different, red,
white, and blue.

00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:48.420
And the gluons are the analog of
the photons of electromagnetism

00:22:48.420 --> 00:22:49.590
that allow--

00:22:49.590 --> 00:22:52.590
that respond to these charges.

00:22:52.590 --> 00:22:55.650
The big difference between QCD
and QED, the big difference

00:22:55.650 --> 00:22:58.620
that comes from having
three colors instead of one,

00:22:58.620 --> 00:23:00.090
is that gluons--

00:23:00.090 --> 00:23:02.160
which can change one
kind of color quark

00:23:02.160 --> 00:23:08.280
into another by carrying
off, say, the green--

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:12.540
excuse me, white-- color
and carrying in a red color,

00:23:12.540 --> 00:23:19.040
thus changing the green one,
the white one, to the red one--

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:21.320
themselves have
unbalanced color charge.

00:23:21.320 --> 00:23:24.830
See, something that does that
has not zero charge, as it

00:23:24.830 --> 00:23:27.230
would be if you had just
one electric charge or you

00:23:27.230 --> 00:23:29.570
changed an electric charge
into an electric charge

00:23:29.570 --> 00:23:30.320
of the same value.

00:23:30.320 --> 00:23:32.880
The photon has zero charge
that it carries off.

00:23:32.880 --> 00:23:34.380
Charge is conserved.

00:23:34.380 --> 00:23:37.370
Here, if you change
one color into another,

00:23:37.370 --> 00:23:39.620
the gluons have
unbalanced charge.

00:23:39.620 --> 00:23:41.760
It has one unit
of green charge--

00:23:41.760 --> 00:23:46.460
white charge-- and minus
one unit of red charge.

00:23:46.460 --> 00:23:53.010
So the gluons themselves carry
the color charge which licenses

00:23:53.010 --> 00:24:00.660
you to draw the
Mercedes-Benz diagram,

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:03.210
where gluons which
respond to color--

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:05.280
that's what they care about--

00:24:05.280 --> 00:24:06.370
interact with each other.

00:24:11.760 --> 00:24:13.530
Many of you have
probably seen Star Wars

00:24:13.530 --> 00:24:16.680
and remember the
laser swordfights.

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:18.750
Well, laser swordfights
would actually

00:24:18.750 --> 00:24:23.460
be very tedious affairs
because if you use photons,

00:24:23.460 --> 00:24:25.690
they'd just wave
through each other.

00:24:25.690 --> 00:24:27.660
Any of you who've
worked in a laser lab

00:24:27.660 --> 00:24:29.550
probably haven't
noticed lasers clinking

00:24:29.550 --> 00:24:32.914
against-- laser light
clinking against each other

00:24:32.914 --> 00:24:34.080
when they happened to cross.

00:24:37.680 --> 00:24:40.530
Of course, it's a movie about a
different galaxy in the future.

00:24:40.530 --> 00:24:45.079
I conjecture that they're
using color lasers with gluons.

00:24:45.079 --> 00:24:46.620
Then something
dramatic would happen.

00:24:46.620 --> 00:24:51.240
I'm not sure exactly what, but
there would be quite a bang.

00:24:51.240 --> 00:24:54.480
Anyway, this changes
the equations,

00:24:54.480 --> 00:24:56.550
it makes them much
more difficult to solve

00:24:56.550 --> 00:25:02.110
and leads to many, many
fascinating phenomena

00:25:02.110 --> 00:25:04.690
that I won't be able
to do justice to,

00:25:04.690 --> 00:25:06.670
of course, in this reflector.

00:25:06.670 --> 00:25:09.130
I'm not even doing justice
to them in my QCD course

00:25:09.130 --> 00:25:10.760
this semester.

00:25:10.760 --> 00:25:18.850
But among the rest, it can be
thought of as mediating forces

00:25:18.850 --> 00:25:21.070
similar to
electromagnetic forces

00:25:21.070 --> 00:25:25.330
that cause quarks to attract
one another, similarly

00:25:25.330 --> 00:25:30.250
to the way that electrons
and protons attract and bind

00:25:30.250 --> 00:25:33.760
each other into atoms.

00:25:33.760 --> 00:25:37.630
Systems of quarks can
attract and bind each other

00:25:37.630 --> 00:25:39.398
into other kinds of particles.

00:25:43.150 --> 00:25:49.070
Well, that's a very imaginative
picture, you may say.

00:25:49.070 --> 00:25:50.710
How do we know
that it's correct?

00:25:50.710 --> 00:25:53.558
And how do we make
it quantitative?

00:25:53.558 --> 00:25:58.950
Well, the key is symmetry.

00:25:58.950 --> 00:26:02.730
Well, the key is
analogy and symmetry.

00:26:02.730 --> 00:26:07.080
As I've told you, there
are deep analogies

00:26:07.080 --> 00:26:12.240
between how gluons
interact with color charges

00:26:12.240 --> 00:26:15.720
and how photons interact
with electromagnetic charges.

00:26:15.720 --> 00:26:18.840
And in fact, we just steal the
equations from electrodynamics

00:26:18.840 --> 00:26:22.260
and use basically the same
equations in this context,

00:26:22.260 --> 00:26:26.150
with the modification that
we have this Mercedes-Benz

00:26:26.150 --> 00:26:26.650
process.

00:26:33.230 --> 00:26:37.300
So we know exactly what the
form of the interactions is.

00:26:37.300 --> 00:26:42.430
And it's postulated to be
perfect symmetry among all

00:26:42.430 --> 00:26:45.080
the different colors.

00:26:45.080 --> 00:26:49.512
So there's no arbitrariness in
how strongly one kind of quark

00:26:49.512 --> 00:26:50.470
interacts with another.

00:26:50.470 --> 00:26:52.360
Every single allowed
process occurs

00:26:52.360 --> 00:26:55.790
with a definitely
determined strength.

00:26:55.790 --> 00:26:59.120
And we have absolutely
unambiguous predictions

00:26:59.120 --> 00:27:03.107
of the theory, if we can just
manage to do the calculations.

00:27:10.262 --> 00:27:17.140
And after something like 10
to the 18th floating point

00:27:17.140 --> 00:27:29.770
operations, you can calculate
with only fundamental

00:27:29.770 --> 00:27:35.630
microscopic input the masses
of protons and neutrons--

00:27:35.630 --> 00:27:38.170
those are called
nucleons on this plot--

00:27:38.170 --> 00:27:41.620
and a whole lot of
other particles made out

00:27:41.620 --> 00:27:44.050
of just the up and
down quarks, the gluons

00:27:44.050 --> 00:27:45.970
that appear in the
strong interaction,

00:27:45.970 --> 00:27:48.010
and there's also
another quark that

00:27:48.010 --> 00:27:49.430
doesn't occur in
ordinary matter,

00:27:49.430 --> 00:27:54.310
but I left it in here to have a
bigger diagram with more things

00:27:54.310 --> 00:27:55.330
to compare--

00:27:55.330 --> 00:27:56.110
the strange quark.

00:28:01.368 --> 00:28:06.280
So these black horizontal
lines-- so we're

00:28:06.280 --> 00:28:10.150
plotting here just different
kinds of particles, and here

00:28:10.150 --> 00:28:12.150
their masses.

00:28:12.150 --> 00:28:13.930
The experimentally
observed masses

00:28:13.930 --> 00:28:17.840
are these horizontal lines.

00:28:17.840 --> 00:28:22.740
And the calculated masses with--

00:28:22.740 --> 00:28:24.750
and this is the
profound point I want

00:28:24.750 --> 00:28:29.130
to emphasize-- no input except
purely conceptual input,

00:28:29.130 --> 00:28:31.530
the nature of the theory
and its symmetries,

00:28:31.530 --> 00:28:36.554
and two mass parameters
for the up and down quarks,

00:28:36.554 --> 00:28:38.220
and if we want to do
strange quarks, one

00:28:38.220 --> 00:28:39.700
more mass parameter.

00:28:39.700 --> 00:28:41.680
This is all output.

00:28:41.680 --> 00:28:45.820
So you compute the
masses of the particles

00:28:45.820 --> 00:28:54.340
here with 10% accuracy in terms
of very, very few parameters.

00:28:54.340 --> 00:28:56.350
By the way, there are
later calculations

00:28:56.350 --> 00:28:58.370
that are beginning to
nibble away at that 10%.

00:28:58.370 --> 00:29:04.270
And there's every reason to
think that the agreement will

00:29:04.270 --> 00:29:04.770
be precise.

00:29:07.920 --> 00:29:10.650
Maybe you have to do 10
to the 20th floating point

00:29:10.650 --> 00:29:13.710
operations instead of 10
to the 18th to get there.

00:29:18.280 --> 00:29:21.700
Underlying this,
these calculations,

00:29:21.700 --> 00:29:28.620
is a vast generalization
of those beautiful pictures

00:29:28.620 --> 00:29:30.850
of the different
states of atoms being

00:29:30.850 --> 00:29:34.950
waves oscillating in space.

00:29:34.950 --> 00:29:39.060
All these different particles
consist of quarks, either three

00:29:39.060 --> 00:29:43.080
quarks or a quark
and an anti-quark,

00:29:43.080 --> 00:29:45.630
oscillating, making
wave patterns like that.

00:29:48.710 --> 00:29:51.770
So they're oscillating in
the same way as electrons,

00:29:51.770 --> 00:29:56.007
but also oscillating in an extra
three dimensional color space.

00:29:56.007 --> 00:29:57.590
The different colors
getting mixed up.

00:29:57.590 --> 00:30:01.950
It really taxes the imagination
to try to think of all this.

00:30:01.950 --> 00:30:07.480
But if you liked those
pictures of hydrogen,

00:30:07.480 --> 00:30:09.210
and if you have a
lot of imagination,

00:30:09.210 --> 00:30:12.070
you would love what
protons look like.

00:30:17.490 --> 00:30:22.590
And in a very precise sense,
the different kinds of particles

00:30:22.590 --> 00:30:23.490
are made up of--

00:30:23.490 --> 00:30:25.698
the different kinds of
particles we observe in nature

00:30:25.698 --> 00:30:27.870
are made out of quarks
and gluons oscillating

00:30:27.870 --> 00:30:30.870
in different ways with the
different waves beating

00:30:30.870 --> 00:30:33.830
against each other
in stable patterns.

00:30:33.830 --> 00:30:35.370
The different
stable patterns are

00:30:35.370 --> 00:30:38.400
what makes the different
particles we observe.

00:30:38.400 --> 00:30:44.220
They are, in a
very precise sense,

00:30:44.220 --> 00:30:50.920
like the tones that
the vacuum can sound,

00:30:50.920 --> 00:30:52.090
that space can sound.

00:30:52.090 --> 00:30:54.730
Space can produce
these particles

00:30:54.730 --> 00:30:57.490
and they interact with each
other in certain stable ways.

00:30:57.490 --> 00:31:02.260
That's exactly how we get tones
from a musical instrument.

00:31:02.260 --> 00:31:05.110
And it's even similar
equations, with waves

00:31:05.110 --> 00:31:06.080
oscillating in space.

00:31:09.290 --> 00:31:12.220
So we get a lot
from very little.

00:31:12.220 --> 00:31:16.990
In fact, the more you look
at this, the more impressive

00:31:16.990 --> 00:31:20.560
it is because the
mass of the gluon

00:31:20.560 --> 00:31:23.537
is taken to be 0,
not for convenience,

00:31:23.537 --> 00:31:25.120
but because the
symmetry of the theory

00:31:25.120 --> 00:31:29.940
requires that the mass of
the gluon be rigorously 0.

00:31:29.940 --> 00:31:34.870
And you notice that the mass
of the up and the down quarks

00:31:34.870 --> 00:31:39.250
in these units isn't making
a negligible contribution

00:31:39.250 --> 00:31:42.160
to the mass of most
of these particles,

00:31:42.160 --> 00:31:44.920
certainly to the proton.

00:31:44.920 --> 00:31:49.480
The mass of the proton is
about 1 in these units, 1 GEV.

00:31:49.480 --> 00:31:51.600
The mass of the
things that are in it

00:31:51.600 --> 00:31:54.440
is contributing almost
nothing to that.

00:31:57.020 --> 00:32:00.600
The mass of the proton doesn't
come from its being made out

00:32:00.600 --> 00:32:03.580
of heavy objects.

00:32:03.580 --> 00:32:06.520
It comes from the fact that
these objects are being bound

00:32:06.520 --> 00:32:08.140
together by attractive forces.

00:32:08.140 --> 00:32:11.404
They're are trying to pull
away because they're waves

00:32:11.404 --> 00:32:13.570
and they want quantum
mechanically to just dissipate

00:32:13.570 --> 00:32:14.070
away.

00:32:14.070 --> 00:32:16.880
But there are forces
pulling them back.

00:32:16.880 --> 00:32:20.560
And so there's energy in the
oscillations, the pull and tug

00:32:20.560 --> 00:32:26.800
between the forces and the
quantum mechanical uncertainty.

00:32:26.800 --> 00:32:31.340
And when you have energy,
according to a slight

00:32:31.340 --> 00:32:33.560
modification of Einstein's
familiar equation--

00:32:33.560 --> 00:32:38.540
not e equals mc squared, but m
equals e divided by e squared--

00:32:38.540 --> 00:32:40.610
you can turn pure
energy into mass.

00:32:40.610 --> 00:32:42.980
And that's, in fact,
the source of most

00:32:42.980 --> 00:32:44.511
of the mass in the universe.

00:32:50.770 --> 00:32:58.250
So really, to do a really
good job on ordinary matter,

00:32:58.250 --> 00:33:00.890
you need you mu,
md, and apparently

00:33:00.890 --> 00:33:02.990
some analog of the
fine structure constant

00:33:02.990 --> 00:33:08.960
that tells you how strongly
the gluons couple, just

00:33:08.960 --> 00:33:12.800
how numerically
powerful the force is.

00:33:12.800 --> 00:33:15.260
But actually, two
of these masses

00:33:15.260 --> 00:33:20.400
are almost insignificant,
quantitatively.

00:33:20.400 --> 00:33:22.800
One sign of that is that
I didn't show arrows here.

00:33:22.800 --> 00:33:24.300
Experimentally,
they're not really

00:33:24.300 --> 00:33:26.680
known to within better
than a factor of two,

00:33:26.680 --> 00:33:29.250
even though they're the most
fundamental constituents

00:33:29.250 --> 00:33:31.200
of matter that have mass.

00:33:36.100 --> 00:33:37.470
But it's even better than that.

00:33:42.630 --> 00:33:44.940
So so far we've gotten
a description of nature,

00:33:44.940 --> 00:33:47.520
of ordinary matter in
terms of five parameters.

00:33:47.520 --> 00:33:52.180
We had the mass of the electron,
the fine structure constant,

00:33:52.180 --> 00:33:54.480
and then we have two that
don't matter very much,

00:33:54.480 --> 00:33:58.140
the masses of the up and down
quarks, and apparently the fine

00:33:58.140 --> 00:34:00.840
structure constant, the
analog of the fine structure

00:34:00.840 --> 00:34:04.830
constant that tells us exactly
how strong the interaction

00:34:04.830 --> 00:34:08.659
between quarks and gluons is.

00:34:08.659 --> 00:34:17.480
But now we come to another
crucial, beautiful aspect

00:34:17.480 --> 00:34:22.360
of QCD, which is that the
strength of the interaction

00:34:22.360 --> 00:34:24.400
depends on the distance
at which you measure it.

00:34:30.300 --> 00:34:34.130
This is due to the fact that in
the quantum mechanical theory,

00:34:34.130 --> 00:34:37.190
you have virtual particles
which come to be and pass away.

00:34:37.190 --> 00:34:41.330
And what we see as empty space
is actually a dynamical medium

00:34:41.330 --> 00:34:44.360
that can screen
charges and affect

00:34:44.360 --> 00:34:46.392
how charges at great
distances see each other.

00:34:46.392 --> 00:34:47.850
They don't see each
other directly,

00:34:47.850 --> 00:34:50.719
but they see each
other as modified

00:34:50.719 --> 00:34:54.070
by the intervening medium.

00:34:54.070 --> 00:34:56.199
So the strength
of the interaction

00:34:56.199 --> 00:34:58.390
depends on the distance.

00:34:58.390 --> 00:35:00.520
It's easier, for
technical reasons,

00:35:00.520 --> 00:35:03.250
to measure how the
probability of radiation

00:35:03.250 --> 00:35:05.960
varies as you change energy.

00:35:05.960 --> 00:35:07.630
But theoretically,
that's the same--

00:35:07.630 --> 00:35:09.760
or the inverse, rather--
of how the force

00:35:09.760 --> 00:35:11.770
changes with the distance.

00:35:11.770 --> 00:35:14.380
And here experimentally you
see a tremendous variety

00:35:14.380 --> 00:35:19.420
of experiments indicating that
as you go to higher energies,

00:35:19.420 --> 00:35:21.250
the probability of
radiating gluons

00:35:21.250 --> 00:35:26.950
goes down, indicating
that the force is getting

00:35:26.950 --> 00:35:29.710
weaker at large
energies or equivalently

00:35:29.710 --> 00:35:31.128
at small distances.

00:35:35.250 --> 00:35:37.920
Or put another way,
the force grows

00:35:37.920 --> 00:35:40.410
as the distance
increases, which is

00:35:40.410 --> 00:35:42.900
an explanation of why
quarks can't get very far

00:35:42.900 --> 00:35:45.200
away from each other.

00:35:45.200 --> 00:35:48.980
In any case, from our sort
of philosophical point

00:35:48.980 --> 00:35:52.940
of perspective of seeing exactly
how much it takes to describe

00:35:52.940 --> 00:35:56.790
the world, the
important phenomenon

00:35:56.790 --> 00:36:03.030
is that we can eliminate
one of the numbers.

00:36:03.030 --> 00:36:05.380
And we've gotten down to five.

00:36:05.380 --> 00:36:07.480
Every step down is
a significant step.

00:36:07.480 --> 00:36:14.760
So we've simplified the
description of the world by 20%

00:36:14.760 --> 00:36:19.170
because we don't have to
specify a fine structure

00:36:19.170 --> 00:36:20.670
constant for the
strong interaction.

00:36:20.670 --> 00:36:23.550
We don't have to specify
how strong it is.

00:36:23.550 --> 00:36:26.020
It can be any strength you want.

00:36:26.020 --> 00:36:28.170
The strength varies
with the distance.

00:36:28.170 --> 00:36:31.560
So I can trade the
strength of the coupling

00:36:31.560 --> 00:36:34.490
for a measure of distance.

00:36:38.737 --> 00:36:40.320
So the strength of
the coupling is not

00:36:40.320 --> 00:36:45.090
an independent parameter in some
sense-- well, in this sense.

00:36:45.090 --> 00:36:48.900
It's simply telling you how
to measure the scale of energy

00:36:48.900 --> 00:36:56.230
or distance because any
value of the coupling

00:36:56.230 --> 00:36:58.570
is actually realized that
some energy or distance.

00:37:12.070 --> 00:37:15.670
So we've gotten mass
without mass, which tells us

00:37:15.670 --> 00:37:25.190
that out of the three apparent
non-conceptual elements of QCD,

00:37:25.190 --> 00:37:27.920
two of them are
pretty insignificant.

00:37:27.920 --> 00:37:32.442
And then a third one is
absolutely insignificant.

00:37:32.442 --> 00:37:33.400
It can be defined away.

00:37:36.030 --> 00:37:39.980
So we've gotten a great deal
the whole structure of protons

00:37:39.980 --> 00:37:42.770
and neutrons and
the masses of nuclei

00:37:42.770 --> 00:37:46.250
practically from pure
concepts from nothing at all.

00:37:46.250 --> 00:37:50.930
But to be accurate, now
our numerical recipe

00:37:50.930 --> 00:37:54.530
contains four elements,
the mass of the electron,

00:37:54.530 --> 00:37:56.857
the fine structure
constant, and the masses

00:37:56.857 --> 00:37:57.940
of the up and down quarks.

00:38:03.110 --> 00:38:06.020
And this gives us a superbly
accurate description

00:38:06.020 --> 00:38:08.300
of ordinary matter.

00:38:08.300 --> 00:38:11.750
It tells us why the thing we
call hydrogen exists and looks

00:38:11.750 --> 00:38:14.190
like hydrogen and has
all its properties,

00:38:14.190 --> 00:38:16.755
why water is what
it is in principle.

00:38:16.755 --> 00:38:18.380
Of course, none of
this we can compute.

00:38:24.260 --> 00:38:25.850
Because of experiments
like the ones

00:38:25.850 --> 00:38:30.860
I alluded to, the fundamental
interactions that we

00:38:30.860 --> 00:38:36.040
can compute, we have great
confidence that the underlying

00:38:36.040 --> 00:38:36.760
theory is sound.

00:38:41.010 --> 00:38:43.640
Well, that and this.

00:38:49.070 --> 00:38:56.950
Now, I want to put in a plug
for physics not being over.

00:38:59.480 --> 00:39:02.840
There's been a lot of-- there
is a tendency to talk loosely

00:39:02.840 --> 00:39:04.532
about the theory of everything.

00:39:07.844 --> 00:39:10.260
And it should be understood
that that's a term of art that

00:39:10.260 --> 00:39:13.070
has a very specific meaning.

00:39:13.070 --> 00:39:15.510
In that sense, I think we do
have a theory of everything

00:39:15.510 --> 00:39:16.650
about ordinary matter.

00:39:16.650 --> 00:39:19.170
We have a very precise
theory with algorithms

00:39:19.170 --> 00:39:22.260
only a very, very small number
of parameters, which I showed

00:39:22.260 --> 00:39:26.520
you, which I think is
going to be our working

00:39:26.520 --> 00:39:28.980
description of matter
for a very long time,

00:39:28.980 --> 00:39:31.280
and probably forever.

00:39:31.280 --> 00:39:33.500
Does that mean we have
a theory of everything

00:39:33.500 --> 00:39:35.660
for ordinary matter?

00:39:35.660 --> 00:39:41.090
No, of course not, because
what it really means

00:39:41.090 --> 00:39:43.631
is that we have nothing more
to tell chemists or biologists

00:39:43.631 --> 00:39:46.130
or something, that everything
we're ever going to tell them,

00:39:46.130 --> 00:39:47.129
we've already told them.

00:39:50.460 --> 00:39:52.090
And there's a
tremendous challenge

00:39:52.090 --> 00:39:56.070
and a tremendous opportunity to
take the fundamentally simple

00:39:56.070 --> 00:40:02.280
laws and build up a description
of nature that really

00:40:02.280 --> 00:40:05.460
does justice to the
complexity and the richness

00:40:05.460 --> 00:40:06.270
of real matter.

00:40:09.600 --> 00:40:13.920
Now we know what the rules are,
we can try to be designers.

00:40:13.920 --> 00:40:16.554
Some of us heard
a brilliant talk

00:40:16.554 --> 00:40:18.720
at lunchtime today by
Professor Joe [? Annopolis, ?]

00:40:18.720 --> 00:40:22.530
who's crafting ways based on
the fundamental laws of physics

00:40:22.530 --> 00:40:24.900
to move light around.

00:40:24.900 --> 00:40:28.680
And that's an
example of exploiting

00:40:28.680 --> 00:40:33.630
our knowledge, our hard won
knowledge, and an example

00:40:33.630 --> 00:40:39.510
of how having the fundamental
laws, in many ways,

00:40:39.510 --> 00:40:42.380
is not the end but the beginning
of challenging problems

00:40:42.380 --> 00:40:42.880
in physics.

00:40:45.590 --> 00:40:47.970
Okay, so much for
ordinary matter.

00:40:51.140 --> 00:40:54.620
We have a quite economical
description of ordinary matter

00:40:54.620 --> 00:40:57.930
that I think Pythagoras would
have been very pleased with.

00:41:01.910 --> 00:41:03.800
Now let's get a
little more ambitious

00:41:03.800 --> 00:41:05.630
and try to do
astrophysics, as well.

00:41:08.160 --> 00:41:12.537
To do astrophysics, I claim we
need just two more parameters.

00:41:20.180 --> 00:41:23.900
One class of processes that's
very important in astrophysics

00:41:23.900 --> 00:41:28.830
are the processes that
cause stars to burn.

00:41:28.830 --> 00:41:32.200
And those are the
weak processes.

00:41:32.200 --> 00:41:36.690
At a fundamental level,
they're described

00:41:36.690 --> 00:41:40.470
in terms of the
possibility of down quarks

00:41:40.470 --> 00:41:44.210
turning into up quarks plus
electrons plus anti neutrinos.

00:41:46.970 --> 00:41:51.660
Or actually, this is the
process of beta decay.

00:41:51.660 --> 00:41:52.640
It's closely related.

00:41:52.640 --> 00:41:54.710
You just bend around
the lines and you

00:41:54.710 --> 00:41:56.897
get the processes
that are responsible

00:41:56.897 --> 00:41:57.730
for stellar burning.

00:42:01.220 --> 00:42:05.600
So this, although it just
looks like a silly picture,

00:42:05.600 --> 00:42:08.720
to a physicist who knows about
relativistic quantum field

00:42:08.720 --> 00:42:12.410
theory, which has
very, very rigid rules,

00:42:12.410 --> 00:42:15.770
is actually associated with
a complete and unambiguous

00:42:15.770 --> 00:42:18.512
description of the
weak interactions.

00:42:22.210 --> 00:42:28.220
And all we need to add
to our numerical recipe

00:42:28.220 --> 00:42:33.560
is one parameter which tells us
about how big this process is,

00:42:33.560 --> 00:42:39.980
how rapidly it occurs over
a one overall new constant.

00:42:39.980 --> 00:42:42.140
And that's called the
Fermi constant, G sub f.

00:42:50.740 --> 00:42:54.920
And then for astrophysics,
the other thing

00:42:54.920 --> 00:42:57.680
that's very important that
we haven't mentioned so far

00:42:57.680 --> 00:42:58.290
is gravity.

00:43:03.430 --> 00:43:09.180
Gravity, you might think,
is, since it's so obvious,

00:43:09.180 --> 00:43:11.490
must be a very powerful
force, and we've

00:43:11.490 --> 00:43:13.120
been silly to be
neglecting it so far.

00:43:16.510 --> 00:43:21.140
However, at a fundamental
level, gravity

00:43:21.140 --> 00:43:24.820
is actually
extravagantly feeble.

00:43:28.120 --> 00:43:33.090
It only wins in
astrophysics by default.

00:43:33.090 --> 00:43:38.790
If you, for instance, compare
the strength of the attraction

00:43:38.790 --> 00:43:41.250
between a proton
and electron due

00:43:41.250 --> 00:43:43.620
to their electrical
interaction, which

00:43:43.620 --> 00:43:47.670
goes like 1 over r squared, to
their gravitational attraction,

00:43:47.670 --> 00:43:49.830
which also goes like
1 over r-squared,

00:43:49.830 --> 00:43:52.620
you'll find that the
electric attraction is

00:43:52.620 --> 00:43:55.410
about 40 orders of
magnitude larger,

00:43:55.410 --> 00:43:57.000
one followed by 40 zeros.

00:44:00.040 --> 00:44:03.820
An extraordinarily large number.

00:44:03.820 --> 00:44:09.699
Physicists like
to put it in terms

00:44:09.699 --> 00:44:11.740
of something called the
hierarchy problem to make

00:44:11.740 --> 00:44:13.450
it quantitative.

00:44:13.450 --> 00:44:15.850
If we want a
quantitative measure

00:44:15.850 --> 00:44:22.860
of how strong gravity
is fundamentally, well,

00:44:22.860 --> 00:44:24.660
we have to ask,
compared to what?

00:44:27.340 --> 00:44:30.570
And since most of the mass
of matter is made in protons,

00:44:30.570 --> 00:44:36.710
we have to construct a
dimensionless quantity,

00:44:36.710 --> 00:44:41.690
a pure number, out of
the honorary numbers,

00:44:41.690 --> 00:44:44.420
Newton's constant and
the mass of the proton.

00:44:44.420 --> 00:44:46.670
And that can be done in
one and only one way.

00:44:46.670 --> 00:44:50.120
And it gives a number, 10
to the minus 38, that tells

00:44:50.120 --> 00:44:54.590
us that gravity in any natural
sense, in a fundamental sense,

00:44:54.590 --> 00:44:57.800
is an extravagantly
feeble force.

00:44:57.800 --> 00:45:00.980
It can dominate in astrophysics
because the other, more

00:45:00.980 --> 00:45:03.770
powerful forces,
being more powerful,

00:45:03.770 --> 00:45:06.620
rearrange matter in such a way
as to cancel each other out

00:45:06.620 --> 00:45:09.290
to reach equilibrium
and neutrality.

00:45:09.290 --> 00:45:12.260
But gravity keeps adding
up, and eventually,

00:45:12.260 --> 00:45:13.610
on large enough scale, wins out.

00:45:27.480 --> 00:45:34.385
Now previously I said
that Planck's constant, h

00:45:34.385 --> 00:45:36.800
bar, and the speed
of light, c, should

00:45:36.800 --> 00:45:39.800
be thought of as
honorary numbers

00:45:39.800 --> 00:45:42.450
because in profound
theories of nature,

00:45:42.450 --> 00:45:43.910
they occur as
conversion factors.

00:45:50.070 --> 00:45:52.680
Now I'd like to argue that
Newton's constant that

00:45:52.680 --> 00:45:58.070
governs the strength of gravity
is also an honorary number.

00:45:58.070 --> 00:46:00.740
That's because it's associated
with the profound theory

00:46:00.740 --> 00:46:03.710
of general relativity
as a conversion factor.

00:46:03.710 --> 00:46:05.990
In general relativity,
there is a relationship

00:46:05.990 --> 00:46:08.210
between the curvature
of space time

00:46:08.210 --> 00:46:12.949
and the energy
density of matter.

00:46:12.949 --> 00:46:14.240
But those have different units.

00:46:14.240 --> 00:46:16.710
The curvature of space-time has
different units from the energy

00:46:16.710 --> 00:46:17.300
of density--

00:46:17.300 --> 00:46:18.470
density of matter.

00:46:18.470 --> 00:46:20.810
We need a conversion
factor to relate them.

00:46:20.810 --> 00:46:23.630
And that conversion factor turns
out to be Newton's constant.

00:46:27.100 --> 00:46:35.960
So if we think that Gn
is an honorary number,

00:46:35.960 --> 00:46:41.000
the question posed by this
extravagantly weakness

00:46:41.000 --> 00:46:47.510
of gravity gets viewed in
a totally different way.

00:46:47.510 --> 00:46:49.900
G Newton is not small.

00:46:49.900 --> 00:46:51.050
It just is what it is.

00:46:51.050 --> 00:46:52.960
It's a conversion--
it's a primary number.

00:46:52.960 --> 00:46:54.210
It's a conversion factor.

00:46:54.210 --> 00:46:58.720
h bar and c, all of them
are honorary numbers.

00:46:58.720 --> 00:46:59.890
They just are what they are.

00:46:59.890 --> 00:47:02.470
There's no way of them
being either large or small.

00:47:02.470 --> 00:47:08.020
So the real question is, why
is the proton mass so light?

00:47:08.020 --> 00:47:10.830
Why is the proton so light?

00:47:15.050 --> 00:47:18.590
Well, why is the
proton so light?

00:47:18.590 --> 00:47:21.230
Well, earlier in the
lecture, I told you

00:47:21.230 --> 00:47:23.630
how the proton gets its mass.

00:47:23.630 --> 00:47:26.610
So we can address the question,
why is the proton so light?

00:47:30.130 --> 00:47:36.930
And the answer is that you
must walk before you run.

00:47:36.930 --> 00:47:38.990
Well, that, I think,
probably sounds

00:47:38.990 --> 00:47:41.040
very cryptic to most of you.

00:47:41.040 --> 00:47:42.290
So let me explain it better.

00:47:47.160 --> 00:47:51.150
As I discussed, the
strength of the interaction

00:47:51.150 --> 00:47:55.350
with which quarks attract each
other depends on the distance.

00:48:00.530 --> 00:48:02.236
And the dependence
is something that we

00:48:02.236 --> 00:48:03.860
can predict theoretically,
and has also

00:48:03.860 --> 00:48:06.110
been measured in a
variety of experiments,

00:48:06.110 --> 00:48:10.850
up to energies of 100 GEV.

00:48:10.850 --> 00:48:13.820
We can extrapolate all the
way to the fundamental energy,

00:48:13.820 --> 00:48:18.200
which, if we believe
that Newton's constant is

00:48:18.200 --> 00:48:22.280
a honorary number,
we can identify as 10

00:48:22.280 --> 00:48:28.610
to the 19th proton masses,
or 10 to the 19th GEV,

00:48:28.610 --> 00:48:30.223
way out here somewhere.

00:48:35.160 --> 00:48:39.750
And the thing that governs
the mass of the proton

00:48:39.750 --> 00:48:41.970
is that at these
distances out here,

00:48:41.970 --> 00:48:44.340
at the fundamental
distances, the forces

00:48:44.340 --> 00:48:48.420
are too weak for quarks to
keep them locked to each other.

00:48:48.420 --> 00:48:50.370
It has to build up.

00:48:50.370 --> 00:48:53.700
But the coupling due to
quantum mechanical fluctuations

00:48:53.700 --> 00:48:56.280
that we talked about, the
screening effect, only

00:48:56.280 --> 00:49:00.840
changes very, very slowly at
first, until a cloud of charge

00:49:00.840 --> 00:49:04.680
builds up and gets
bigger and bigger.

00:49:04.680 --> 00:49:05.462
So it's walking.

00:49:05.462 --> 00:49:06.920
It's actually sort
of limping along

00:49:06.920 --> 00:49:10.940
like a wounded snail
for a long time,

00:49:10.940 --> 00:49:13.640
until it slowly builds up.

00:49:13.640 --> 00:49:19.760
And then finally, at, of course,
not coincidentally, a length

00:49:19.760 --> 00:49:21.962
corresponding to the
mass of the proton,

00:49:21.962 --> 00:49:24.170
it becomes strong enough to
bind the quarks together.

00:49:28.120 --> 00:49:31.810
That's why protons are so
light in natural units.

00:49:31.810 --> 00:49:35.740
It comes about because the
coupling was a little bit

00:49:35.740 --> 00:49:37.956
small at the fundamental scale.

00:49:37.956 --> 00:49:39.580
And given that it's
a little bit small,

00:49:39.580 --> 00:49:42.760
it takes a long, long
time for the small quantum

00:49:42.760 --> 00:49:45.790
mechanical effects to
build up and make it big

00:49:45.790 --> 00:49:47.329
and eventually bind protons--

00:49:47.329 --> 00:49:48.370
bind quarks into protons.

00:50:08.200 --> 00:50:11.580
Now, as I said, so
now we've introduced--

00:50:11.580 --> 00:50:17.690
we have a description
of matter which

00:50:17.690 --> 00:50:22.380
is a very accurate description,
including both ordinary matter

00:50:22.380 --> 00:50:26.280
and astrophysics, based on six
quantities-- the fine structure

00:50:26.280 --> 00:50:30.420
constant, the mass of
the electron, the masses

00:50:30.420 --> 00:50:35.460
of the up and down quarks, the
Newton constant, and the Fermi

00:50:35.460 --> 00:50:36.280
constant.

00:50:36.280 --> 00:50:40.650
They're the things that
appear in red on your program.

00:50:40.650 --> 00:50:43.860
But I've just been trying
to actually improve.

00:50:43.860 --> 00:50:46.140
I said each time you make
an improvement on that,

00:50:46.140 --> 00:50:49.570
you're making a major
contribution to physics.

00:50:49.570 --> 00:50:55.320
So I've just been trying to
implement the idea, if you

00:50:55.320 --> 00:50:59.370
like, or discuss the idea that
Planck's constant, too, should

00:50:59.370 --> 00:51:01.130
be regarded as an
honorary number.

00:51:05.620 --> 00:51:09.430
And we scored a significant
success for that point of view

00:51:09.430 --> 00:51:13.060
by explaining how the
proton could be so absurdly

00:51:13.060 --> 00:51:20.000
light measured in
those natural units,

00:51:20.000 --> 00:51:22.880
or putting it another way,
why gravity is so feeble.

00:51:27.820 --> 00:51:30.710
Now, if that explanation--

00:51:30.710 --> 00:51:33.770
if we're going to succeed
in actually promoting

00:51:33.770 --> 00:51:43.330
the Newton constant
to an honorary number

00:51:43.330 --> 00:51:47.980
and reduce our
numerical recipe, it

00:51:47.980 --> 00:51:51.940
has to work not only
for QCD, but also

00:51:51.940 --> 00:51:53.770
for the other
interactions in the world.

00:51:53.770 --> 00:51:55.690
Or let me put it another way.

00:51:55.690 --> 00:52:03.590
We would like to see that same
scale, that Newton constant,

00:52:03.590 --> 00:52:06.820
emerge in some
other way in physics

00:52:06.820 --> 00:52:10.730
that's independent of
the theory of gravity.

00:52:10.730 --> 00:52:17.110
Well, remarkably enough,
there is another way

00:52:17.110 --> 00:52:19.000
in which the Newton
constant emerges

00:52:19.000 --> 00:52:20.990
from quite different
considerations

00:52:20.990 --> 00:52:22.630
in our fundamental
theories of physics.

00:52:29.240 --> 00:52:32.670
As I told you, the couplings
change with distance very,

00:52:32.670 --> 00:52:34.010
very slowly.

00:52:34.010 --> 00:52:37.100
Here, to make the
plot look simple

00:52:37.100 --> 00:52:39.620
and be able to fit it
on one little sheet,

00:52:39.620 --> 00:52:42.240
we've switched to
a logarithmic scale

00:52:42.240 --> 00:52:46.100
and plotted inverse couplings
instead of couplings.

00:52:46.100 --> 00:52:50.210
And I have here the fine
structure constant for QCD,

00:52:50.210 --> 00:52:52.340
the fine structure constant
for electrodynamics,

00:52:52.340 --> 00:52:55.280
and an analogous thing that
occurs in the weak interactions

00:52:55.280 --> 00:52:57.920
that I haven't described,
but is something that is

00:52:57.920 --> 00:53:01.620
important in particle physics.

00:53:01.620 --> 00:53:05.430
And you can ask if all these
different interactions that we

00:53:05.430 --> 00:53:09.240
see at low energies might
be different manifestations

00:53:09.240 --> 00:53:16.700
of a unified theory that
is simple in its operations

00:53:16.700 --> 00:53:19.700
at short distances, but
gets obscured from us

00:53:19.700 --> 00:53:21.920
by these same quantum
mechanical fluctuations

00:53:21.920 --> 00:53:25.095
and screening effects that
make the couplings change

00:53:25.095 --> 00:53:25.710
with distance.

00:53:29.020 --> 00:53:32.860
So operationally, we have
to take these guys from

00:53:32.860 --> 00:53:34.870
experiment-- that's
where we measure them--

00:53:34.870 --> 00:53:36.790
and then theoretically
calculate what

00:53:36.790 --> 00:53:39.310
the effect of the screening
is to see if they could have

00:53:39.310 --> 00:53:42.170
derived from a unified theory.

00:53:42.170 --> 00:53:49.200
And remarkably enough,
the measured values

00:53:49.200 --> 00:53:51.210
are consistent
with their emerging

00:53:51.210 --> 00:53:54.120
from a unified theory
where they all become equal

00:53:54.120 --> 00:53:57.780
and all become different
facets of one interaction.

00:53:57.780 --> 00:54:01.880
And that occurs at
an energy that's

00:54:01.880 --> 00:54:07.100
very similar to the energy
we extract, the Planck scale

00:54:07.100 --> 00:54:10.220
we extract, from Newton's
constant, this 10

00:54:10.220 --> 00:54:11.420
to the 19th GEV.

00:54:21.980 --> 00:54:26.660
So if we ask, could there be
a unified theory of matter,

00:54:26.660 --> 00:54:32.420
we get the resounding
answer that yes,

00:54:32.420 --> 00:54:35.060
not only could there be, but
there's a strong indication

00:54:35.060 --> 00:54:38.380
that the very different
looking interactions

00:54:38.380 --> 00:54:41.350
we see at low energies are
all facets of one unified

00:54:41.350 --> 00:54:42.430
theory at high energies.

00:54:45.190 --> 00:54:51.470
And if we do
further experiments,

00:54:51.470 --> 00:54:56.120
further discoveries-- including
the existence of neutrino mass,

00:54:56.120 --> 00:55:01.010
which, in its details, supports
the idea of such unified

00:55:01.010 --> 00:55:02.440
theories--

00:55:02.440 --> 00:55:05.090
the unified theories
also predict

00:55:05.090 --> 00:55:06.730
that protons should decay.

00:55:06.730 --> 00:55:09.200
That one hasn't
been observed yet.

00:55:09.200 --> 00:55:12.470
So we get two exclamation
points and a question

00:55:12.470 --> 00:55:17.570
mark to our question, is there
a unified theory of matter

00:55:17.570 --> 00:55:22.148
that congeals at something
close to this Planck scale.

00:55:30.130 --> 00:55:33.640
But then the final step must
be to bring back in gravity.

00:55:36.360 --> 00:55:40.530
Well, gravity is also sensitive
to the energy at which you

00:55:40.530 --> 00:55:44.530
measure, and not just
because of subtle quantum

00:55:44.530 --> 00:55:47.890
mechanical effects, but
because gravity just

00:55:47.890 --> 00:55:50.240
cares about energy.

00:55:50.240 --> 00:55:54.280
The gravitational force is
proportional to mass or energy,

00:55:54.280 --> 00:55:59.540
according to e
equals mc squared.

00:55:59.540 --> 00:56:02.200
So the higher the energy,
the stronger gravity

00:56:02.200 --> 00:56:06.250
appears relative to
the other interactions.

00:56:06.250 --> 00:56:08.970
And so the inverse
coupling of gravity

00:56:08.970 --> 00:56:12.490
on this logarithmic scale
happens to look like that.

00:56:12.490 --> 00:56:15.120
And you can see
that gravity also

00:56:15.120 --> 00:56:17.100
seems to be joining
the other interactions.

00:56:17.100 --> 00:56:19.230
We can't do this
calculation very accurately,

00:56:19.230 --> 00:56:23.070
but to the accuracy
that it deserves,

00:56:23.070 --> 00:56:26.760
it's consistent with the idea
that all these interactions

00:56:26.760 --> 00:56:27.570
unite together.

00:56:31.190 --> 00:56:36.260
So the basic idea
that Newton's constant

00:56:36.260 --> 00:56:39.950
can be regarded as
an honorary number,

00:56:39.950 --> 00:56:45.290
and should be the
fundamental mass that

00:56:45.290 --> 00:56:48.770
appears in the fundamental
unified theory,

00:56:48.770 --> 00:56:53.030
holds up very well from two
very different perspectives.

00:56:53.030 --> 00:57:00.170
It's the scale at which
there's independent indication

00:57:00.170 --> 00:57:01.850
of a fundamental
theory of emerging

00:57:01.850 --> 00:57:04.050
of the non-gravitational forces.

00:57:04.050 --> 00:57:09.630
And it's also the
scale at which gravity

00:57:09.630 --> 00:57:14.220
meets those and potentially
a fully unified theory that

00:57:14.220 --> 00:57:16.140
includes not just
a theory of matter,

00:57:16.140 --> 00:57:18.540
but also the theory of
space and time, which

00:57:18.540 --> 00:57:25.920
is what gravity is in Einstein's
general relativity theory.

00:57:25.920 --> 00:57:29.640
So to the question, do
these considerations

00:57:29.640 --> 00:57:34.500
of the numerical
recipe for nature point

00:57:34.500 --> 00:57:39.970
us toward a unified theory
of space-time matter,

00:57:39.970 --> 00:57:40.830
this one does.

00:57:44.460 --> 00:57:46.890
But really, that's the only
quantitative indication

00:57:46.890 --> 00:57:50.730
so far along those lines.

00:57:50.730 --> 00:57:52.290
And there are big
puzzles in trying

00:57:52.290 --> 00:57:54.870
to construct a unified
theory with gravity

00:57:54.870 --> 00:57:56.710
and the other interactions.

00:57:56.710 --> 00:58:00.960
There's the puzzle of why empty
space doesn't weigh anything.

00:58:00.960 --> 00:58:02.580
And there's just
the puzzle that we

00:58:02.580 --> 00:58:05.010
don't have any very concrete
theory along these lines.

00:58:07.910 --> 00:58:09.860
There are the germs
of ideas coming

00:58:09.860 --> 00:58:12.890
from string theory that
perhaps will congeal

00:58:12.890 --> 00:58:15.080
into a well-defined theory.

00:58:15.080 --> 00:58:18.230
But at present, it's kind of
a vague assemblage of ideas.

00:58:25.160 --> 00:58:28.640
So let me summarize.

00:58:28.640 --> 00:58:33.450
To construct ordinary matter,
to construct a description

00:58:33.450 --> 00:58:37.800
of ordinary matter that's
extremely precise and very well

00:58:37.800 --> 00:58:43.510
verified, we were able to get
by with a couple of honorary

00:58:43.510 --> 00:58:52.410
numbers, h bar and c, and
four non-numerical quantities,

00:58:52.410 --> 00:58:53.820
exactly four--

00:58:53.820 --> 00:58:56.970
the mass of the electron,
the fine structure constant,

00:58:56.970 --> 00:59:00.190
and the masses of the
ups and down quarks.

00:59:00.190 --> 00:59:02.830
And among those, the masses of
the up quarks and down quarks

00:59:02.830 --> 00:59:07.390
didn't matter very
much quantitatively.

00:59:07.390 --> 00:59:11.090
If we want to do
astrophysics as well,

00:59:11.090 --> 00:59:14.700
we needed to add just
two more numbers--

00:59:14.700 --> 00:59:17.710
the Fermi constant describing
the weak interactions

00:59:17.710 --> 00:59:20.590
and the Newton's
constant describing

00:59:20.590 --> 00:59:23.060
the strength of gravity.

00:59:23.060 --> 00:59:26.510
And then finally,
I gave you a series

00:59:26.510 --> 00:59:31.460
of arguments sort of at
the frontiers of physics

00:59:31.460 --> 00:59:34.550
indicating that the idea that
we can treat Newton's constant

00:59:34.550 --> 00:59:41.090
also as an honorary number is
becoming very, very plausible.

00:59:41.090 --> 00:59:43.310
We get at that number
from considering

00:59:43.310 --> 00:59:45.560
unified theories of
the other interactions

00:59:45.560 --> 00:59:47.990
and how they emerge.

00:59:47.990 --> 00:59:50.750
We get a convincing
explanation of why

00:59:50.750 --> 00:59:56.570
gravity is so feeble based on
interpreting it as actually

00:59:56.570 --> 00:59:58.190
the lightness of protons--

00:59:58.190 --> 01:00:00.800
which in turn was
interpreted as the coupling

01:00:00.800 --> 01:00:04.160
having to walk before it runs--

01:00:04.160 --> 01:00:08.600
and then finally from the
just straight calculation

01:00:08.600 --> 01:00:11.964
of whether gravity unifies
with the other interactions.

01:00:15.836 --> 01:00:33.180
So the Pythagorean
vision that the world

01:00:33.180 --> 01:00:40.170
can be described in
terms of pure numbers

01:00:40.170 --> 01:00:42.300
is very, very close
to being realized

01:00:42.300 --> 01:00:45.110
in a very concrete
and beautiful way

01:00:45.110 --> 01:00:47.140
that I hope I've given
you some inkling of.

01:00:47.140 --> 01:00:49.140
Thank you.

01:00:49.140 --> 01:00:52.640
[APPLAUSE]

01:00:59.140 --> 01:01:03.196
PRESENTER: I'm sure Frank
will answer questions.

01:01:03.196 --> 01:01:05.691
WILCZEK: Yes.

01:01:05.691 --> 01:01:06.689
AUDIENCE: Thanks.

01:01:06.689 --> 01:01:11.180
Since you talked about
[INAUDIBLE] very troublesome

01:01:11.180 --> 01:01:21.145
[INAUDIBLE] We have no
theoretical explanation

01:01:21.145 --> 01:01:22.630
or description.

01:01:22.630 --> 01:01:26.095
And that area of
physics [INAUDIBLE]

01:01:26.095 --> 01:01:28.570
to what you called very
briefly [INAUDIBLE]??

01:01:40.680 --> 01:01:42.360
WILCZEK: Well, yes.

01:01:45.740 --> 01:01:48.500
I tried to dissociate
myself very carefully

01:01:48.500 --> 01:01:52.160
from the philosophy,
if you want to call it

01:01:52.160 --> 01:01:56.480
that, that in physics, you're
done once you write down

01:01:56.480 --> 01:01:57.538
the equations.

01:02:00.926 --> 01:02:02.300
It's an important
part of physics

01:02:02.300 --> 01:02:03.860
to write down the equations.

01:02:03.860 --> 01:02:06.090
But to really be
able to solve them

01:02:06.090 --> 01:02:09.110
in meaningful circumstances,
to be able to do them justice,

01:02:09.110 --> 01:02:12.350
to relate them to the
world, is a tremendous art,

01:02:12.350 --> 01:02:14.600
and every bit as
important and challenging

01:02:14.600 --> 01:02:18.365
as finding the equations.

01:02:18.365 --> 01:02:19.820
Yes.

01:02:19.820 --> 01:02:24.190
AUDIENCE: Electron has
a charge and the quarks

01:02:24.190 --> 01:02:26.870
have charges of
one third and 2/3

01:02:26.870 --> 01:02:30.810
and they exactly match, how
does that come out of your

01:02:30.810 --> 01:02:32.220
[INAUDIBLE]?

01:02:32.220 --> 01:02:38.480
WILCZEK: Oh, well that
does actually come out of--

01:02:38.480 --> 01:02:43.270
so the question
was, if you actually

01:02:43.270 --> 01:02:47.590
look in detail at some of
the properties of our quarks

01:02:47.590 --> 01:02:49.900
and electrons, they're
a little funny.

01:02:49.900 --> 01:02:53.410
For instance, the electric
charge of the up quark

01:02:53.410 --> 01:02:57.420
has to be 2/3 the
electric charge of--

01:02:57.420 --> 01:03:02.080
or minus 2/3 the electric
charge of the electron.

01:03:02.080 --> 01:03:04.510
And the electric charge
of the down quark

01:03:04.510 --> 01:03:08.570
is one third the electric
charge of the electron.

01:03:08.570 --> 01:03:10.970
Where did these funny numbers
like 2/3 and one third

01:03:10.970 --> 01:03:12.260
come from?

01:03:12.260 --> 01:03:15.080
Well, first of all,
since they're numbers,

01:03:15.080 --> 01:03:16.490
they're not anti-Pythagorean.

01:03:19.110 --> 01:03:22.890
But secondly, and
more seriously,

01:03:22.890 --> 01:03:25.606
they are among the most--

01:03:25.606 --> 01:03:27.420
I haven't been able
to do it justice.

01:03:27.420 --> 01:03:30.460
And I won't be able to do it
justice in this brief lecture.

01:03:30.460 --> 01:03:34.890
But they emerge in a
very compelling way

01:03:34.890 --> 01:03:36.090
from these unified theories.

01:03:39.576 --> 01:03:41.786
Let's see, how can I say
this in a simple way?

01:03:46.250 --> 01:03:55.330
You see-- yeah.

01:03:55.330 --> 01:03:58.610
The physical photon,
as we observe it,

01:03:58.610 --> 01:04:02.540
is some mixture of the gluons
in the fundamental theory.

01:04:02.540 --> 01:04:05.280
And so are the gluons of
the strong interaction.

01:04:05.280 --> 01:04:06.560
They are mixtures.

01:04:06.560 --> 01:04:09.590
And which particular
mixtures emerge as the photon

01:04:09.590 --> 01:04:11.660
and emerge as the
color gluons is

01:04:11.660 --> 01:04:14.555
determined by the details
of how this symmetry breaks,

01:04:14.555 --> 01:04:17.960
of how the big symmetry of
the original underlying theory

01:04:17.960 --> 01:04:20.140
breaks.

01:04:20.140 --> 01:04:23.440
So to address questions
like the relative charges

01:04:23.440 --> 01:04:26.980
of different objects,
we need to be specific

01:04:26.980 --> 01:04:32.590
about what this theory was, and
about how the original, highly

01:04:32.590 --> 01:04:36.580
symmetrical theory
broke down into the less

01:04:36.580 --> 01:04:41.120
symmetrical theories we
actually see at low energies.

01:04:41.120 --> 01:04:44.036
I can be a little bit
more specific about this

01:04:44.036 --> 01:04:45.660
and give you some
idea of how it works.

01:04:45.660 --> 01:04:49.680
But to really do it would
require some equations.

01:04:49.680 --> 01:04:53.580
I emphasized that the
theory of electrodynamics

01:04:53.580 --> 01:04:58.020
was based on very similar
concepts to the theory of QCD.

01:04:58.020 --> 01:05:00.870
They were both based on
different kinds of charges,

01:05:00.870 --> 01:05:03.780
also called colors, and
their transformations

01:05:03.780 --> 01:05:10.790
and interactions with
photons or gluons.

01:05:10.790 --> 01:05:13.850
The form of this
unified theory--

01:05:13.850 --> 01:05:16.280
oh, and I should say, the
theory of the weak interaction

01:05:16.280 --> 01:05:20.140
is based on a similar idea
involving two other colors.

01:05:20.140 --> 01:05:22.657
So all these theories
are different kinds of--

01:05:22.657 --> 01:05:24.240
theories of different
kinds of charges

01:05:24.240 --> 01:05:26.880
interacting with
different kinds of gluons.

01:05:26.880 --> 01:05:30.690
The unified theory is simply
including all possible

01:05:30.690 --> 01:05:33.250
transformations among all
the colors-- strong, weak,

01:05:33.250 --> 01:05:35.430
and electromagnetic--

01:05:35.430 --> 01:05:40.650
and seeing if they can be
incorporated on equal footing.

01:05:40.650 --> 01:05:43.430
And the calculation here
shows that that idea succeeds.

01:05:49.110 --> 01:05:52.910
Then you have to discuss,
well, why isn't the world--

01:05:52.910 --> 01:05:56.330
why in the real world don't
we see all these interactions

01:05:56.330 --> 01:05:57.240
on an equal footing?

01:05:57.240 --> 01:06:00.030
What happened?

01:06:00.030 --> 01:06:01.680
And that's the subject--

01:06:01.680 --> 01:06:05.800
the phenomenon is called
spontaneous symmetry breaking.

01:06:05.800 --> 01:06:11.630
And it will sound poetic,
but it's literally the case

01:06:11.630 --> 01:06:14.450
that what's involved
here is the concept

01:06:14.450 --> 01:06:18.890
that the whole world is a
multi-layered, multicolored

01:06:18.890 --> 01:06:21.230
superconductor.

01:06:21.230 --> 01:06:25.850
Ordinary superconductors
are governed by the concept

01:06:25.850 --> 01:06:28.760
that you have so-called
Cooper pairs of electrons,

01:06:28.760 --> 01:06:37.550
pairing up and filling a metal
and giving a photon a mass

01:06:37.550 --> 01:06:39.890
and effecting the
properties of photons,

01:06:39.890 --> 01:06:43.640
effectively giving photons a
mass inside superconductors.

01:06:43.640 --> 01:06:48.520
In these theories, what we
need is not pairs of electrons,

01:06:48.520 --> 01:06:52.010
as in superconductors, but
pairs of similar things

01:06:52.010 --> 01:06:54.990
carrying other kinds
of color charges,

01:06:54.990 --> 01:06:58.000
filling what we think
of as empty space.

01:06:58.000 --> 01:07:00.110
But of course, it's not empty.

01:07:00.110 --> 01:07:02.900
It's a multi-layered,
multicolored superconductor

01:07:02.900 --> 01:07:06.610
because it has these pairs.

01:07:06.610 --> 01:07:09.170
It's filled chock-a-block
with pairs of particles

01:07:09.170 --> 01:07:10.460
with different colors.

01:07:10.460 --> 01:07:13.280
And it's the presence
of that medium that

01:07:13.280 --> 01:07:17.600
distinguishes the different
colors between strong

01:07:17.600 --> 01:07:18.650
electromagnetic and weak.

01:07:18.650 --> 01:07:25.262
Say these pairs have more--

01:07:25.262 --> 01:07:26.734
are more aligned
in the direction

01:07:26.734 --> 01:07:28.900
of the weak interaction
than the strong interaction,

01:07:28.900 --> 01:07:31.070
and that distinguishes
the two directions

01:07:31.070 --> 01:07:32.650
and breaks the symmetry.

01:07:35.996 --> 01:07:39.770
Well, I'm trying
to say something

01:07:39.770 --> 01:07:41.370
that's easier done than said.

01:07:41.370 --> 01:07:51.340
But the-- well,
maybe I'm giving you

01:07:51.340 --> 01:07:54.160
some sense that it's the
details of how this symmetry is

01:07:54.160 --> 01:07:57.880
broken that determines the
charges at the end of the day.

01:07:57.880 --> 01:08:02.440
And if you take sort of the
simplest possibilities for how

01:08:02.440 --> 01:08:05.290
this symmetry is broken,
that's what gives you

01:08:05.290 --> 01:08:07.300
the structures we
observe at low energies,

01:08:07.300 --> 01:08:10.600
including things
like the charge 2/3

01:08:10.600 --> 01:08:14.720
and one third on the quarks
that otherwise seem so funny.

01:08:14.720 --> 01:08:15.315
Yeah.

01:08:15.315 --> 01:08:17.315
AUDIENCE: It seems that
you're being [INAUDIBLE]

01:08:17.315 --> 01:08:19.210
the question I had
since the early slide

01:08:19.210 --> 01:08:20.850
when you were showing the pairs.

01:08:20.850 --> 01:08:23.680
There are paired
reds, paired blues,

01:08:23.680 --> 01:08:26.669
but no green pair on that slide.

01:08:26.669 --> 01:08:27.169
Is that

01:08:27.169 --> 01:08:28.463
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

01:08:28.463 --> 01:08:29.129
WILCZEK: Gluons?

01:08:29.129 --> 01:08:30.599
Oh, yes.

01:08:30.599 --> 01:08:35.009
Well, yeah, totally unorganized.

01:08:35.009 --> 01:08:41.109
[LAUGHTER]

01:08:41.109 --> 01:08:43.189
So you might think,
if we have gluons

01:08:43.189 --> 01:08:46.180
that change any possible
color into any other color,

01:08:46.180 --> 01:08:47.979
including the same
one, that there

01:08:47.979 --> 01:08:50.130
would be nine possibilities,
three times three.

01:08:52.649 --> 01:08:56.399
And there are, of course.

01:08:56.399 --> 01:09:02.069
But one of those
colored gluons, well,

01:09:02.069 --> 01:09:04.800
the joke I might like to make
is that these are gauge bosons.

01:09:04.800 --> 01:09:06.716
But one of them
is a gauge bogon.

01:09:06.716 --> 01:09:07.215
It's bogus.

01:09:10.660 --> 01:09:13.990
There's one that's
different from all the rest.

01:09:13.990 --> 01:09:16.450
And it's composed of
an equal combination

01:09:16.450 --> 01:09:19.210
of the red, anti-red,
blue, anti-blue,

01:09:19.210 --> 01:09:22.858
and white, anti-white,
or green, anti-green.

01:09:22.858 --> 01:09:24.399
In quantum mechanics,
you are allowed

01:09:24.399 --> 01:09:28.189
to take linear combinations of
these different possibilities.

01:09:28.189 --> 01:09:36.520
And the gluon which treats
all those colors symmetrically

01:09:36.520 --> 01:09:39.300
obviously has
different properties

01:09:39.300 --> 01:09:41.790
than any of these
other guys which

01:09:41.790 --> 01:09:44.810
don't treat the different
colors symmetrically.

01:09:44.810 --> 01:09:46.760
If you know a
little group theory,

01:09:46.760 --> 01:09:48.830
if you take a
product of a triplet

01:09:48.830 --> 01:09:51.170
and an anti-triplet
representation of color, which

01:09:51.170 --> 01:09:54.470
is what we have here, they
form an octet, eight gluons,

01:09:54.470 --> 01:09:56.810
which is perfectly
symmetrical, and a singlet,

01:09:56.810 --> 01:09:59.490
which has different properties.

01:09:59.490 --> 01:10:01.580
So in the theory of
the strong interaction,

01:10:01.580 --> 01:10:04.110
that singlet
doesn't participate.

01:10:04.110 --> 01:10:05.330
It's different from the rest.

01:10:08.190 --> 01:10:10.790
And so to enforce
the proper symmetry

01:10:10.790 --> 01:10:13.080
of the strong interaction
and agree with nature,

01:10:13.080 --> 01:10:16.520
it's consistent and
necessary to throw it out.

01:10:16.520 --> 01:10:19.520
So actually, it's a slight lie--

01:10:19.520 --> 01:10:20.740
well, it's a big lie--

01:10:20.740 --> 01:10:24.140
to just leave out the
green, anti-green.

01:10:24.140 --> 01:10:30.080
What I should have written here
was red, anti-red minus blue,

01:10:30.080 --> 01:10:34.240
anti-blue and something
like blue, anti-blue minus

01:10:34.240 --> 01:10:35.247
green, anti-green.

01:10:35.247 --> 01:10:36.830
Then it would have
been mathematically

01:10:36.830 --> 01:10:41.101
correct but probably
even more confusing.

01:10:41.101 --> 01:10:41.600
Yes.

01:10:44.468 --> 01:10:47.336
AUDIENCE: Your graph of
the various [INAUDIBLE]

01:10:47.336 --> 01:10:52.468
versus energy, it looks
on the low energy side

01:10:52.468 --> 01:10:58.546
as if you're changing the
fine structure constant

01:10:58.546 --> 01:11:01.536
by a few percent every decade.

01:11:01.536 --> 01:11:04.464
WILCZEK: This is-- wait, wait.

01:11:04.464 --> 01:11:05.440
This one.

01:11:10.320 --> 01:11:12.290
This one?

01:11:12.290 --> 01:11:16.161
AUDIENCE: No, you had the quark,
the three different coupling

01:11:16.161 --> 01:11:16.660
constants.

01:11:16.660 --> 01:11:17.040
WILCZEK: Yes.

01:11:17.040 --> 01:11:19.240
AUDIENCE: The straight and
the gravity was [INAUDIBLE]..

01:11:19.240 --> 01:11:19.420
WILCZEK: Right.

01:11:19.420 --> 01:11:21.200
AUDIENCE: So if I
just extrapolate

01:11:21.200 --> 01:11:23.430
that down a few more
orders of magnitude,

01:11:23.430 --> 01:11:25.660
then I raise the
question, why do I

01:11:25.660 --> 01:11:29.390
see nine decimal
places, the same fine

01:11:29.390 --> 01:11:34.170
structure constant in hydrogen
and in singly ionized helium?

01:11:34.170 --> 01:11:36.120
WILCZEK: You don't.

01:11:36.120 --> 01:11:41.400
I mean, when you do accurate
calculations of the force

01:11:41.400 --> 01:11:43.890
between, say, electrons--

01:11:43.890 --> 01:11:49.900
between an electron and
a positron or whatever,

01:11:49.900 --> 01:11:54.370
I guess you find that the force
does change logarithmically.

01:11:54.370 --> 01:11:57.130
This is the Uehling effect
or vacuum polarization which

01:11:57.130 --> 01:11:59.330
appears in atomic physics.

01:11:59.330 --> 01:12:00.600
So--

01:12:00.600 --> 01:12:02.975
AUDIENCE: I'm aware of that,
but it's a whole lot flatter

01:12:02.975 --> 01:12:05.330
and straight per decade so
something must be happening

01:12:05.330 --> 01:12:06.760
is my question.

01:12:06.760 --> 01:12:07.510
WILCZEK: Yeah.

01:12:07.510 --> 01:12:13.000
Well, these calculations
are done basically

01:12:13.000 --> 01:12:14.860
neglecting the
masses of particles

01:12:14.860 --> 01:12:17.130
relative to the energy.

01:12:17.130 --> 01:12:19.460
And that's valid for all
the particles we know

01:12:19.460 --> 01:12:21.780
about sort of from here on out.

01:12:21.780 --> 01:12:23.750
But it would be totally invalid.

01:12:23.750 --> 01:12:25.000
AUDIENCE: So they flatten out?

01:12:25.000 --> 01:12:26.540
WILCZEK: Yeah, they flatten out.

01:12:26.540 --> 01:12:29.510
Well, they flatten out
in these two cases.

01:12:29.510 --> 01:12:37.170
In this case, well,
it's not exactly known.

01:12:37.170 --> 01:12:38.790
It becomes a strong
coupling problem.

01:12:38.790 --> 01:12:40.260
And it's not really
well-defined.

01:12:40.260 --> 01:12:44.410
But anyway, yeah, you can't
just extrapolate these curves.

01:12:44.410 --> 01:12:45.460
That's quite right.

01:12:45.460 --> 01:12:46.197
Yes.

01:12:46.197 --> 01:12:48.280
AUDIENCE: If we use this
slide and the convergence

01:12:48.280 --> 01:12:50.770
of these curves to
sort of try to dub

01:12:50.770 --> 01:12:54.230
a couple of your constants
into honorary numbers--

01:12:54.230 --> 01:12:56.510
WILCZEK: Just [INAUDIBLE].

01:12:56.510 --> 01:12:57.140
AUDIENCE: Okay.

01:12:57.140 --> 01:12:59.820
But don't you get if you--

01:12:59.820 --> 01:13:01.656
WILCZEK: So the
question is, can--

01:13:01.656 --> 01:13:02.280
well, go ahead.

01:13:02.280 --> 01:13:03.693
Ask your question.

01:13:03.693 --> 01:13:04.635
[LAUGHTER]

01:13:04.635 --> 01:13:06.990
I'll ask the question
you should be asking.

01:13:10.649 --> 01:13:13.190
AUDIENCE: I guess what I mean
is I have a feeling that you've

01:13:13.190 --> 01:13:18.180
somehow got one more honorary
than you're really entitled to.

01:13:18.180 --> 01:13:20.570
I mean, for instance,
alpha s, you

01:13:20.570 --> 01:13:23.100
turned that into an honorary
number by saying, well, really,

01:13:23.100 --> 01:13:25.295
lambda QCD just sets
the length scale.

01:13:25.295 --> 01:13:27.115
It's sort of the
natural unit of length.

01:13:27.115 --> 01:13:28.490
But then the Planck
length you're

01:13:28.490 --> 01:13:30.500
trying to tell me is the
natural unit of length.

01:13:30.500 --> 01:13:31.970
I mean, can't you only use one--

01:13:31.970 --> 01:13:34.970
WILCZEK: Yes, I did do somewhat
of a sleight of hand here.

01:13:34.970 --> 01:13:37.760
If I make the Planck
length the scale of length

01:13:37.760 --> 01:13:42.170
and run through my explanation
of why gravity is feeble

01:13:42.170 --> 01:13:46.670
or why protons are so
light, that explanation

01:13:46.670 --> 01:13:49.760
required knowing what
the value of alpha s

01:13:49.760 --> 01:13:51.790
was at the Planck length.

01:13:51.790 --> 01:13:56.050
So if I do it that
way, I reintroduce

01:13:56.050 --> 01:13:59.032
a numerical parameter.

01:13:59.032 --> 01:14:00.526
So you're quite right, yes.

01:14:04.012 --> 01:14:06.502
Yeah.

01:14:06.502 --> 01:14:10.070
AUDIENCE: I'm actually speaking
with the voice of Pythagoras.

01:14:10.070 --> 01:14:13.490
If you can show me
your Pythagoras thing,

01:14:13.490 --> 01:14:18.179
we have noticed that you have an
error in your numerical table.

01:14:18.179 --> 01:14:19.570
WILCZEK: Oh, is that?

01:14:19.570 --> 01:14:22.926
AUDIENCE: You could leave it
as an exercise for the audience

01:14:22.926 --> 01:14:25.283
to figure out what the error is.

01:14:25.283 --> 01:14:25.866
WILCZEK: Okay.

01:14:30.312 --> 01:14:36.740
AUDIENCE: The error is that the
ratio of e to c is actually,

01:14:36.740 --> 01:14:41.520
I worked it out here, 81 to 64.

01:14:41.520 --> 01:14:43.420
Any violinist understands that.

01:14:43.420 --> 01:14:44.390
WILCZEK: Oh, well.

01:14:44.390 --> 01:14:49.240
[LAUGHTER]

01:14:49.240 --> 01:14:50.210
[INTERPOSING VOICES]

01:14:50.210 --> 01:14:52.720
AUDIENCE: It is a terrible
scale because everything

01:14:52.720 --> 01:14:53.698
sounds dissonant.

01:14:56.770 --> 01:14:57.315
[INAUDIBLE]

01:14:57.315 --> 01:14:59.606
WILCZEK: I believe it's the
scale that Pythagoras used.

01:14:59.606 --> 01:15:00.564
AUDIENCE: No, it's not.

01:15:00.564 --> 01:15:01.486
It's not.

01:15:01.486 --> 01:15:01.986
No.

01:15:05.794 --> 01:15:10.020
The ratio of e to c is 81 to 64.

01:15:10.020 --> 01:15:11.934
WILCZEK: You mean a to the gap?

01:15:15.350 --> 01:15:16.761
Well, I don't know.

01:15:16.761 --> 01:15:17.260
Okay.

01:15:17.260 --> 01:15:18.468
AUDIENCE: It's a music thing.

01:15:18.468 --> 01:15:20.080
WILCZEK: I don't
know this history.

01:15:20.080 --> 01:15:20.580
But--

01:15:20.580 --> 01:15:24.294
AUDIENCE: If you can find
a hint related to it,

01:15:24.294 --> 01:15:29.502
[INAUDIBLE] where you'll
find that the magic ratio

01:15:29.502 --> 01:15:33.718
God made when he made the
world, the ratio was 256 to 243.

01:15:33.718 --> 01:15:37.622
[INAUDIBLE]

01:15:37.622 --> 01:15:38.600
WILCZEK: All right.

01:15:38.600 --> 01:15:42.130
Well, for those of you
who didn't catch this,

01:15:42.130 --> 01:15:44.680
let me just remark
that 81 divided by 64

01:15:44.680 --> 01:15:47.110
is very close to five.

01:15:47.110 --> 01:15:49.510
[LAUGHTER]

01:15:52.111 --> 01:15:54.610
PRESENTER: On that note, I think
we should thank Frank again

01:15:54.610 --> 01:15:55.210
for--

01:15:55.210 --> 01:15:58.560
[APPLAUSE]

